SPEC §5, §7 5b + "The bridge", §8. Role::Upstream requires status (Future -> {reachable, phase, via, ...}) and endpoints (Future -> [Endpoint]); optional replicate_into($comb). Upstream::Static: fixed endpoints, no cluster (Docker, vendors, tests), optional phase/via. Upstream::K8s: read-only get of the peer Comb CR in another kube context (context; namespace and name default to the own ones); client for that context built like the Comb own client (sync or async); missing/inaccessible context or missing CR -> reachable false with reason, never an exception; cluster address when both contexts point at the same API server, else external; none -> unreachable; via = [context, @peer status.upstream.via]. reconcile 5b: upstream status + endpoints, optional replicate_into, bridge_manifests -> deploy -> prune (local resources no longer rendered get pruned); bridge ok AND upstream Running -> Running; reachable but not Running -> Pending with reason; unreachable -> Blocked with reason; status.upstream and status.endpoints (resolved, redirected) written; endpoint($name) returns the redirected address. Bridge per endpoint: hostname -> Service type ExternalName; IP (v4 and v6) -> selector-less Service + EndpointSlice (discovery.k8s.io/v1, label kubernetes.io/service-name). Corners: ExternalName cannot remap ports - if the upstream port differs from the local port, never deploy a silently broken bridge (report it); switching a local ClusterIP Service named like the endpoint to ExternalName must work (same name in both sets, updated in place, no clusterIP carried over); a via chain containing this Comb own context is a loop -> Blocked. The CR only ever holds the fully qualified upstream class name.

